WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.414 --> 00:00:04.004
Unit six. Screen Time Balance!

2
00:00:04.967 --> 00:00:09.324
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.374 --> 00:00:12.735
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:12.785 --> 00:00:16.791
Today we learn about Screen Time Balance. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.441 --> 00:00:22.736
Screen time. Say it with me. Screen time!

6
00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:30.386
Balance. Say it with me. Balance!

7
00:00:33.874 --> 00:00:37.565
Break. Say it with me. Break!

8
00:00:41.064 --> 00:00:45.789
Outside play. Say it with me. Outside play!

9
00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:54.025
Rest your eyes. Say it with me. Rest your eyes!

10
00:00:57.486 --> 00:01:01.920
Healthy habit. Say it with me. Healthy habit!

11
00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:09.263
Timer. Say it with me. Timer!

12
00:01:12.762 --> 00:01:17.512
Family time. Say it with me. Family time!

13
00:01:21.006 --> 00:01:34.656
Screen time should have a good balance with outside play and family time. I take a break and rest my eyes after using a screen for a while. Using a timer helps me build a healthy habit.

14
00:01:34.706 --> 00:01:38.078
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:38.819 --> 00:01:44.251
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:44.301 --> 00:01:45.451
Break!

17
00:01:46.291 --> 00:01:51.766
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:51.816 --> 00:01:52.966
Timer!

19
00:01:53.937 --> 00:02:00.531
Did you know? Looking at something far away for 20 seconds every 20 minutes can help rest your eyes!

20
00:02:00.581 --> 00:02:02.773
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:03.776 --> 00:02:12.596
Think and answer. What do you like to do when you take a break from a screen?

22
00:02:12.646 --> 00:02:13.796
Great answer!

23
00:02:14.772 --> 00:02:20.958
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:21.008 --> 00:02:24.032
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

